# Visualizar una serie temporal {#sec-visualising data-tr-id="u9381a7" data-tr-status="machine" data-tr-reviews="0"}

[El primer paso de cualquier tarea de pronóstico es graficar los datos. Un gráfico temporal muestra las observaciones frente al tiempo y hace visibles la tendencia y la estacionalidad.]{.tr data-tr-id="uc0165e" data-tr-status="machine" data-tr-reviews="0"}


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(ggplot2)

# Convertir la serie mensual en un data frame para graficar
passengers <- data.frame(
  month = seq(as.Date("1949-01-01"), by = "month", length.out = length(AirPassengers)),
  count = as.numeric(AirPassengers)
)

ggplot(passengers, aes(x = month, y = count)) +
  geom_line(colour = "steelblue") +
  labs(
    title = "Pasajeros aéreos",
    x = "Mes",
    y = "Pasajeros (miles)"
  )
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![Monthly international airline passengers, 1949–1960.](visualising_files/figure-html/fig-passengers-1.png){#fig-passengers width=672}
:::
:::


[@fig-passengers shows a clear upward trend. The seasonal pattern also grows
with the level of the series: the summer peaks become larger every year.]{.tr data-tr-id="u459485" data-tr-status="missing" data-tr-reviews="0" lang="en"}

## Seasonal plots {#sec-seasonal-plots data-tr-id="u277ec2" data-tr-status="missing" data-tr-reviews="0" lang="en"}

[A seasonal plot draws each year as a separate line, so that the shape of the
seasonal pattern is easier to compare from one year to the next.]{.tr data-tr-id="u6e489a" data-tr-status="missing" data-tr-reviews="0" lang="en"}


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# One line per year, coloured from earliest to latest
passengers$year <- format(passengers$month, "%Y")
passengers$month_of_year <- as.integer(format(passengers$month, "%m"))

ggplot(passengers, aes(x = month_of_year, y = count, group = year, colour = year)) +
  geom_line() +
  scale_x_continuous(breaks = 1:12, labels = month.abb) +
  labs(x = "Month of the year", y = "Passengers (thousands)", colour = "Year")
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![Each year of the series drawn as its own line.](visualising_files/figure-html/fig-seasonal-1.png){#fig-seasonal width=672}
:::
:::


[July and August are the busiest months in every year of the data.]{.tr data-tr-id="u0aa05a" data-tr-status="missing" data-tr-reviews="0" lang="en"}
